tamp`), the response code (`response`), size in bytes, client IP, URL, source and destination country, OS, and user agent.\n\n**Dashboard: \"EFF-eed22ab9 Web logs overview\"** has 7 panels, at http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-eed22ab9-web-logs-overview-a72aad53edda\n- **Totals:** total requests, unique visitors (counted by client IP), and total bytes served.\n- **Requests over time:** a bar chart split by the top 5 response codes.\n- **Response code breakdown:** a pie chart.\n- **Top 10 URLs:** a table with request count and bytes for each.\n- **Top 10 source countries:** a bar chart of requests.\n\n**Alert rule: \"EFF-eed22ab9 5xx spike\"** (id `6eca4419-4dfa-418c-922f-1fa2b12e8580`)\n- It is an Elasticsearch query rule on `kibana_sample_data_logs`. It checks every minute and fires when more than 10 requests in the last 5 minutes have a response code starting with \"5\".\n- It assumes `response.keyword` stores codes as text like \"503\". If it doesn't, the rule will never fire. You can check this by searching `response.keyword:5*` in Discover.\n- The rule is switched on but has no notification attached, so when it fires it only records an alert in Kibana. Add a connector (email, Slack, etc.) if you want to be told.","ttft_ms":2024,"type":"result","duration_ms":43097,"uuid":"e05ee692-ea84-4fb7-92b0-4387f9cec5af","ttft_stream_ms":1739,"time_to_request_ms":95,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":23,"system_prompt":9,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":11,"input_hooks":6,"tool_pool_refresh":2,"init_message":2,"engine_pickup":2,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":11,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":6,"request_build":12},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":45,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":126,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"queued_commands","slowest_producer_ms